      "writtenOn": "2026-07-06T02:58:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this wrapper can hand out dangling references. `\u0027v` is a free parameter (only in `PhantomData`), and `try_from` builds the value from `unchecked_frozen_value().to_value()` with an unconstrained `\u0027v`.\n\nFor a borrowing `T` like `\u0026str` or `Value\u003c\u0027v\u003e`, `deref` lets safe code copy the inner value out (`let s: \u0026str \u003d *assert.eval::\u003c\u0026str\u003e(...)`); the temporary then drops its `FrozenHeapRef` and `s` dangles. The safety comment assumes the heap outlives `T`, but the two lifetimes are not actually tied. \n\nShould we restrict this to owned `T`, or reuse starlark\u0027s `OwnedFrozenValueTyped` / `downcast_starlark`, which bundle the keep-alive safely?",
      "revId": "3bc39ffe71f1584c5bc2feaa951d8f83d2b48cbd",
